From: ObliviOS Build <build@oblivios.local>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 21:25:18 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] telephony: bring the copy of CellSubset up to its source

CellSubset gained placeIds (frameworks-base/0018, for the automatic place); the copy in the Telephony
app stays equal to its source, as tools/check-copies.py requires. The app does not call the method.
---
 src/com/android/phone/CellSubset.java | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/com/android/phone/CellSubset.java b/src/com/android/phone/CellSubset.java
index 6cd2209..28b9fc4 100644
--- a/src/com/android/phone/CellSubset.java
+++ b/src/com/android/phone/CellSubset.java
@@ -6,6 +6,7 @@ import java.util.Collections;
 import java.util.HashMap;
 import java.util.List;
 import java.util.Map;
+import java.util.Set;
 
 /**
  * The cell towers of the persona (ADR-208): a few towers per place of {@link Places}, with the operator codes of the country,
@@ -110,6 +111,11 @@ final class CellSubset {
         return first.mcc + (first.mnc < 10 ? "0" : "") + first.mnc;  // not String.format: the digits would follow the locale
     }
 
+    /** The ids of the places that have at least one cell. */
+    Set<Integer> placeIds() {
+        return Collections.unmodifiableSet(byPlace.keySet());
+    }
+
     /** At most 8 cells of the place in file order; empty for a place without cells. */
     List<Cell> cellsFor(int placeId) {
         List<Cell> all = byPlace.get(placeId);
